  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nToday will be another warm day, with highs in the upper 60s to \nlower 70s for most of the area. Even with mostly cloudy\nconditions and rain showers ahead of an approaching cold front,\ntemperatures remain warm.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nThe aforementioned cold front will move through the region on\ntoday, with widespread rain showers this morning and then drying\nout later this afternoon. \n\nMost of the area should stay dry Friday, with possibly showers \ncontinuing across the Poconos and southern Catskills as a wave \nof low pressure tracks along the Mid Atlantic Coast. Shower \npotential will increase again Saturday morning from west to \neast, as the upper level low tracks into the area and slowly \npushes through, with isolated to scattered showers lingering \nuntil Sunday morning.\n\nAnother trough dropping southeast out of Canada will bring \nanother chance for showers late Sunday night into Monday, with \nlake enhancement adding to the shower potential.",
